# Local tooling drops: agent scratch, editor session state, recording caches.
# These belong on this disk only — and they are not decoration: measured on this
# checkout on 2026-10-12 with the app's own walk rules, 16,968 of the 17,360
# source-shaped files under the repository live in these folders, against 392 in
# the project itself, so a folder scan of this
# repository would read tooling output as the developer's code unless the rule
# lives in the file git actually ships.
.qoder-scratch/
/.qoder/
.hermes/
**/.video_agent/
.zcode/

# Handoffs between the roles that build this: plans, review axes, test
# walkthroughs. They quote machine-local paths and the internal voice of a
# working session, so they stay on this disk and never reach a reader.
/_handoffs/

# Raw measurement dumps from the multi-role review runs (ledger CSV + screenshots).
# Durable statements are folded into docs/UI_REVIEW.md; the dumps stay local.
docs/reviews/

# The three working documents of the pre-publication pass, named one by one
# rather than as a folder so the next person can still add a real doc under docs/.
# They speak in the voice of the session that wrote them — a review that states
# "nothing has been published", a strategy memo, an acceptance protocol — and
# each of those sentences turns wrong the moment the repository is public. Their
# durable content already lives in README.md, docs/UI_REVIEW.md and CONTRIBUTING.md,
# and the screenshots the review cites went to docs/reviews/ beside the other
# local-only dumps, because docs/assets/ may hold nothing a document does not link.
docs/RELEASE_REVIEW_2026-10-11.md
docs/WORKING_BACKWARDS_2026.md
docs/WORLD_EXPERIENCE_ACCEPTANCE.md

# Credential carriers. The app never reads a key file, so nothing here needs
# one; these rules exist for the day someone drops a real one next to the code
# while testing a scanner. `.env` and `.env.*` above already cover the dotfile
# forms; the rest are the key-material formats and the ssh/netrc files that are
# named the same way on every machine. Public keys (`.pub`) stay committable.
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx
*.p12
*.kdbx
id_rsa
id_ed25519
id_ecdsa
id_dsa
.netrc
_netrc
